From 157886ddcd591e68ce4edef6eccad6a4772040a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:32:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg: the decoder of both views is not asked
 to skip pictures

A player that is very late asks the decoder to skip the pictures that
nothing refers to (skip_frame), packet by packet. Some Matroska files
hold the second view of an access unit in the packet of the base view of
the next one: the request then skips one view of an access unit and not
the other, and the decoder gives a second view together with the base
view of another time, under the time of that one. What pairs the views
in Kodi goes by their times and cannot tell.

Measured on a host, with the decoder driven as Kodi drives it and its
output compared with a clean decode of each view: with skipping on some
packets, 61 of the 185 pictures of one conformance stream had the second
view of another time as their right half; with one access unit a packet,
and without skipping in either layout, none had.

The decoder of both views is no longer asked to skip. A player that is
late drops pictures after they are decoded, as it does for any stream
when that is not enough.
---
 .../VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp  | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
index 04d7dd2..b3579e8 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -2128,6 +2128,15 @@ void CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg::SetCodecControl(int flags)
     else
       m_requestSkipDeint = false;
 
+    // Hades: the decoder of both views is never asked to skip pictures. A packet may hold the
+    // second view of one access unit and the base view of the next (some Matroska files have
+    // them so), and the request holds for a packet: one view of an access unit is skipped
+    // without the other, and the decoder then gives a second view with the base view of
+    // another time, under the time of that one. A player that is late drops pictures after
+    // they are decoded instead.
+    if (m_multiview)
+      bDrop = false;
+
     if (bDrop)
     {
       m_pCodecContext->skip_frame = AVDISCARD_NONREF;
-- 
2.53.0

